# Copy to .env (ignored) and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# Optional: without it, `proxenos web` asks for your name, the vault and a model on first run, and
# keeps settings in ~/Library/Application Support/Proxenos/settings.json and keys and tokens in the
# macOS Keychain (on Windows, %APPDATA%\Proxenos\settings.json and Credential Manager; on Linux,
# ~/.config/proxenos/settings.json and the Secret Service). Running from source with an .env, it's
# read first and the page writes to it.

# Settings are PROXENOS_*. Older TWIN_* names are still read when the new one isn't set.

# The private vault: raw exports, the self-model, briefs, evals.
# Must be outside this repo, which is public.
PROXENOS_VAULT=~/proxenos_vault

# The model. An open one on this Mac needs no key and sends nothing out: install Ollama's app
# (brew install --cask ollama-app && open -a Ollama), pull a model (ollama pull gemma4:26b,
# about 17 GB, fits a 32 GB Mac) and name it here. Or leave it unset and use a personal
# Anthropic API key (console.anthropic.com), separate from any work account.
PROXENOS_MODEL=ollama:gemma4:26b
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# What you wait on (Ask, Think, an errand, a call) can go to another model, Claude say, while
# the night stays on the one above: PROXENOS_ASK_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5, with the key set.
PROXENOS_ASK_MODEL=

# Or a model another app serves on this computer through OpenAI's API: PROXENOS_MODEL=local:<name>,
# the name its /v1/models lists, at PROXENOS_LOCAL_URL. Empty: LM Studio's http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1.
# llama.cpp's llama-server is at http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1 and vLLM at http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1.
# Only this computer's own address (localhost, 127.0.0.0/8, ::1) is used; any other is refused.
# Load the model there with a context of 65536 tokens (llama-server -c 65536).
# PROXENOS_LOCAL_URL=

# Optional. Search by meaning embeds with this Ollama model (`proxenos index --vectors`), even
# when the model above is on another server, and a voice model trained on your own writing
# drafts replies (docs/voice-model.md): "mlx" for `proxenos voice serve`, or "ollama:<name>" or
# "local:<name>". Empty: no voice model.
# PROXENOS_EMBED_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:0.6b
# PROXENOS_VOICE_MODEL=

# A project's steps (`proxenos clone steps`): what does the work on its code. Empty: Claude Code
# where it's installed, on the account it's signed in to (never the key above), then the local
# model, which can only write. Or "claude" or "local". The budget is the most one step may spend,
# in dollars. PROXENOS_STEP_MODEL names Claude Code's model (empty: its own default);
# PROXENOS_CLAUDE_BIN is where Claude Code is when it isn't on the PATH or in /opt/homebrew/bin;
# PROXENOS_WORKTREES is where steps' worktrees go (empty: beside the settings file).
PROXENOS_STEP_RUNNER=
PROXENOS_STEP_BUDGET=5
PROXENOS_STEP_MODEL=
PROXENOS_CLAUDE_BIN=
PROXENOS_WORKTREES=

# Your projects as folders in a cloud drive you already sync here (Google Drive for desktop,
# Dropbox, OneDrive, iCloud Drive), to read, edit, comment on and share in Word or Google Docs
# (`proxenos clone folders`, each night). A folder that's there, e.g. ~/Library/CloudStorage/
# GoogleDrive-you@gmail.com/My Drive/Projects. Each project's manuscript and Proxenos's notes on
# it go there as Word files, which your drive uploads, and what you change in a Markdown
# manuscript comes back as a step for you to accept. Empty: nothing is written. pandoc makes
# the files (`brew install pandoc`); PROXENOS_PANDOC is where it is when it isn't on the PATH.
# tectonic makes the PDFs (`brew install tectonic`); PROXENOS_TECTONIC is where it is.
PROXENOS_PROJECT_FOLDER=
# PROXENOS_PANDOC=
# PROXENOS_TECTONIC=

# What Proxenos calls you in its notes and self-model.
PROXENOS_NAME=

# Public mentions and published work (news search, OpenAlex). PROXENOS_OPENALEX_ID pins the author
# profile (e.g. A123...) if the name search picks the wrong one.
PROXENOS_FULL_NAME=
PROXENOS_OPENALEX_ID=

# Bluesky handle for reading your public posts.
PROXENOS_BLUESKY_HANDLE=

# Gmail over IMAP, one line per account: GMAIL_<NAME>=address:app-password. NAME names the
# stream (raw/email/<name>). App passwords: myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (needs 2-Step
# Verification); IMAP must be on in Gmail settings. Where app passwords aren't allowed, put a
# Google Cloud "Desktop app" OAuth client below and run `proxenos auth gmail NAME ADDRESS` (or
# sign in from the page's Connect view), which writes GMAIL_<NAME>=address:oauth:<refresh token>
# here.
GMAIL_PERSONAL=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Google Calendar, live: the same Google client, with the Google Calendar API on in its project.
# `proxenos auth gcalendar NAME ADDRESS` (or the Connect view) asks only to read the calendar and
# writes GCALENDAR_<NAME>=address:oauth:<refresh token> here.

# Google Docs, for a project's manuscript: the same Google client, with the Google Drive API on in
# its project. `proxenos auth gdocs NAME ADDRESS` (or the Connect view) asks only for drive.file,
# the files Proxenos makes, and writes GDOCS_<NAME>=address:oauth:<refresh token> here.

# Microsoft 365 and Outlook.com mail and calendar, through Microsoft Graph. Register your own app
# in the Azure portal (Microsoft Entra ID, App registrations): accounts in any organizational
# directory and personal Microsoft accounts, redirect URI http://localhost under "Mobile and
# desktop applications", no client secret. Put its Application (client) ID here, then run
# `proxenos auth microsoft NAME ADDRESS` (or use the Connect view), which writes
# MICROSOFT_<NAME>=address:oauth:<refresh token> here.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=

# Your addresses across all accounts, comma-separated, so email knows which mail is yours.
PROXENOS_EMAILS=

# Strava: an app at strava.com/settings/api and a refresh token with activity:read_all.
# After the first run the latest token lives in the vault and this one can be removed.
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
STRAVA_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Spotify, live: your latest plays every sync. Make an app at developer.spotify.com (Dashboard,
# Create app, Web API) with http://127.0.0.1:8723/callback as its redirect URI, put its Client ID
# here, then run `proxenos auth spotify`, which saves the refresh token. No secret is needed.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Slack: either slackdump archives (no token needed; see PROXENOS_SLACKDUMP_DIR below), or a
# user OAuth token (xoxp-...) from an app at api.slack.com/apps with these user scopes:
# channels:read groups:read im:read mpim:read channels:history groups:history im:history
# mpim:history users:read. Leave token rotation off.
SLACK_USER_TOKEN=

# Sources that live in folders on your computer. A leading ~ is expanded. With the Spotify or
# website setting empty, `proxenos sync` and `proxenos night` skip that source.

# Spotify: the folder of your Extended Streaming History export (the one holding
# Streaming_History_Audio_*.json). `proxenos ingest spotify --export DIR` reads another folder
# for one run, and `proxenos import` picks up a fresh download without this setting.
PROXENOS_SPOTIFY_EXPORT=

# Letterboxd: your username. Sync reads your public diary feed, the last 50 or so films you
# logged, so new ones come in without an export. Empty: only exports are read.
PROXENOS_LETTERBOXD_USER=

# Plans from your messages (a lunch at 12) go on this calendar in the Mac's Calendar app, as
# it names it (your Google one, say me@gmail.com), which syncs them to its account. Only the
# events Proxenos made are ever changed or deleted. Empty: only /api/plans.ics, to subscribe to.
PROXENOS_PLANS_CALENDAR=

# Your website: its local git repo, whose pages, posts and CV data are read.
# `proxenos ingest website --repo DIR` reads another repo for one run.
PROXENOS_WEBSITE_REPO=

# slackdump: a folder holding slackdump_* runs. The repo's data/ folder is searched as well, so
# leave this empty if you drop the runs there.
PROXENOS_SLACKDUMP_DIR=

# Optional. PROXENOS_BIN is the path to the proxenos command, for when the page can't find it
# on PATH (it runs it to rebuild the people index).
# PROXENOS_BIN=

# Optional. When `proxenos schedule` runs each job: minutes between syncs (0 for none), and the
# local time of the nightly run (off for none). --sync-every and --night-at override them.
# PROXENOS_SYNC_EVERY=15
# PROXENOS_NIGHT_AT=01:30

# Instagram, Messenger, X and LinkedIn chats, live, through Beeper Desktop's local API: a token
# from Beeper (Settings, Integrations). See docs/data_sources.md.
BEEPER_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Calls (docs/calls.md): your own Twilio account's SID and auth token (or save them in the
# page's Settings), the Twilio number that rings you, your own number verified in Twilio as
# the caller ID the other side sees (else the Twilio number), your phone, which it rings, and
# the address Tailscale Funnel gives the call server. Optional: the model on a call, if not
# PROXENOS_MODEL.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
PROXENOS_TWILIO_NUMBER=
PROXENOS_CALLER_ID=
PROXENOS_PHONE=
PROXENOS_CALLS_URL=
# PROXENOS_CALL_MODEL=

# Notices on your phone through ntfy (https://ntfy.sh, open source): install its app on Android
# or iOS, subscribe to a topic with a long random name, and put that name here (or save it in the
# page's Settings). Empty: no notices. When sync or night finds more drafts to send, care items,
# project steps to review or tasks due soon than before, one notice says how many of each, and
# nothing else: never a name, a message's words, a subject or a health detail. On ntfy.sh anyone
# who knows the topic can read it, so treat it like a password. NTFY_TOKEN is only for a server
# with access control. PROXENOS_NTFY_SERVER is your own server (empty: https://ntfy.sh), and
# PROXENOS_QUIET_HOURS when a notice waits instead, in local time (empty: 22:00-08:00; off for
# none). `proxenos notify test` sends a test notice.
NTFY_TOPIC=
# NTFY_TOKEN=
# PROXENOS_NTFY_SERVER=
# PROXENOS_QUIET_HOURS=22:00-08:00

# Folders of documents read every sync, comma-separated (a health records folder, say).
PROXENOS_DOCS_DIRS=

# Errands: more folders to look in for your CV, comma-separated (it already looks in the folders
# above, your downloaded exports and ~/Documents), and the address Mail sends an errand's email
# from (its default account when empty).
# PROXENOS_CV_DIRS=
# PROXENOS_MAIL_FROM=

# Looking people up (`proxenos lookup email "NAME" --org ORG`): when an errand, Ask or Think needs
# someone's email address and your records have none, that person's name and where they are go
# to a search engine, and only that organization's own public pages among the results are read;
# nothing about you. The engine is your own SearXNG when PROXENOS_SEARXNG_URL names it (with json
# among its search formats), else Brave Search's API with BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY (a key from
# api-dashboard.search.brave.com), else DuckDuckGo. PROXENOS_LOOKUP=off stops it.
PROXENOS_SEARXNG_URL=
BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY=
# PROXENOS_LOOKUP=off
